[Claim 1]
A driving assistance device comprising:
a vehicle information storage unit that acquires and stores other vehicle time-series information transmitted from vehicles operating within a communication range with the vehicle via a vehicle-to-vehicle communication device;
an motion state estimation unit that estimates the motion state of the other vehicle based on the stored other vehicle time-series information;
a correction target interval detection unit that, when:
the reliability information contained in the other vehicle time-series information stored in the vehicle information storage unit is below a predetermined threshold value, and
this state persists for a duration longer than a predetermined time interval,
detects the interval during which the reliability information remains below the predetermined threshold as a correction target interval and outputs it to the motion state estimation unit; and
an motion state correction unit that:
simulates the other vehicle's trajectory based on the estimated motion state of the other vehicle, and
outputs the simulated trajectory of the other vehicle;
where the motion state includes:
time-series horizontal orientation information, velocity information, acceleration information, and angular velocity information of the vehicle's orientation;
the motion state estimation unit estimates the motion state of the other vehicle while it is traveling through the correction target interval input from the correction target interval detection unit;
the motion state correction unit generates correction candidates for each piece of information contained in the other vehicle's motion state, corrects the motion state, and calculates an alignment evaluation value between the simulated trajectory of the other vehicle and map information containing lane information; and
the device is characterized by outputting the trajectory with the highest alignment with the map information based on the calculated alignment evaluation value.
